WAN Failover Plugin

Decides when an IPv4 WAN leaves service and when it comes back, moves
connections to the right WAN both ways, and restarts Tailscale only when
the default route actually changed.

- A WAN whose dpinger loss exceeds the gateway's own threshold, or that is
  hard down, is held with force_down while another WAN is usable; once
  held it returns only when a settled window shows no loss at all
- Never both: a hold needs a usable alternative and is released at once
  on positive evidence that the alternative failed
- A reboot releases every hold before routing starts
- A new hold kills that WAN's states; when a WAN recovers, flows that
  prefer it move back once their rule and the default route point there
- Ownership (which gateways it holds) is saved with force_down in one
  config write, so a config backup carries both

